# The PQMS docs corpus is hand-wrapped: line breaks, column alignment and
# table padding are authored deliberately. Letting Prettier reflow this
# markdown destroys the tables and rewrites every line, which turns
# `git blame` into a single useless commit for the whole file.
# 14-code-style-and-linting.md states the same rule: "Prettier ignores **/*.md".
**/*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VENDORED BYTE-COPIES AND GENERATED FILES — never reformat.
#
# These are not style exemptions. They are files this project does not own:
# byte-copies of the design system's shipped output, and generated artefacts
# whose producer decides their formatting. Reformatting any of them breaks the
# thing that verifies them.
#
# Measured, not assumed: `prettier --check` reports that EVERY path below would
# be rewritten today. Without these lines, one `prettier --write .` silently
# corrupts the vendored adherence ruleset and every design-system byte-copy, and
# tokens:check / the generated-file drift gate would then fail against files
# nobody knowingly edited.
_adherence.oxlintrc.json
packages/design-tokens/design-system-manifest.json
packages/design-tokens/src/styles/design-system/**
packages/design-tokens/src/tokens/tokens.generated.ts

# Build output, dependencies, lockfiles, binary captures.
**/dist/**
node_modules/**
pnpm-lock.yaml
.fidelity/**

